{
 "duration": 189.44,
 "cues": [
  {
   "id": "h1",
   "scene": "hook",
   "show": "One link. A whole company shares it.",
   "start": 1.0,
   "end": 3.23
  },
  {
   "id": "h2",
   "scene": "hook",
   "show": "Lunch hour. Everyone wants it at once.",
   "start": 3.65,
   "end": 6.01
  },
  {
   "id": "h3",
   "scene": "hook",
   "show": "Something has to slow down.",
   "start": 6.43,
   "end": 7.7
  },
  {
   "id": "h4",
   "scene": "hook",
   "show": "So\u2026 who would YOU slow down?",
   "start": 8.22,
   "end": 9.8
  },
  {
   "id": "p1",
   "scene": "problem",
   "show": "Network slicing splits one network into reserved virtual lanes, called slices.",
   "start": 13.82,
   "end": 17.72
  },
  {
   "id": "p2",
   "scene": "problem",
   "show": "We built a real testbed: 7 departments, 7 slices, one 1-megabit link.",
   "start": 18.09,
   "end": 23.13
  },
  {
   "id": "p3",
   "scene": "problem",
   "show": "950 kilobits are usable, but 1,480 were promised.",
   "start": 23.5,
   "end": 27.67
  },
  {
   "id": "p4",
   "scene": "problem",
   "show": "That's normal, like a gym selling more memberships than machines.",
   "start": 28.04,
   "end": 30.99
  },
  {
   "id": "p5",
   "scene": "problem",
   "show": "Normal networks decide with technical labels, set at install time.",
   "start": 31.56,
   "end": 34.86
  },
  {
   "id": "p6",
   "scene": "problem",
   "show": "The canteen screens are tagged URLLC, premium. The regulated quality lab, eMBB, standard.",
   "start": 35.23,
   "end": 41.65
  },
  {
   "id": "p7",
   "scene": "problem",
   "show": "So the network slows the lab\u2026 and protects the lunch menu.",
   "start": 42.07,
   "end": 44.88
  },
  {
   "id": "s1",
   "scene": "solution",
   "show": "Our software ignores labels and asks business questions.",
   "start": 45.8,
   "end": 48.37
  },
  {
   "id": "s2",
   "scene": "solution",
   "show": "How critical is it? What does a minute of outage cost?",
   "start": 48.74,
   "end": 51.59
  },
  {
   "id": "s3",
   "scene": "solution",
   "show": "Factory line: \u00a38,400. Canteen screens: \u00a315.",
   "start": 51.91,
   "end": 56.77
  },
  {
   "id": "s4",
   "scene": "solution",
   "show": "Safety rules? Customer impact? How long can it cope? Was it slowed recently?",
   "start": 57.19,
   "end": 62.88
  },
  {
   "id": "l0",
   "scene": "loop",
   "show": "Then a 7-step loop runs every 2 seconds.",
   "start": 63.8,
   "end": 65.89
  },
  {
   "id": "l1",
   "scene": "loop",
   "show": "1. Measure real traffic, delay and lost data at the gateway.",
   "start": 66.41,
   "end": 70.13
  },
  {
   "id": "l2",
   "scene": "loop",
   "show": "2. Detect: demand over 102% of the link, twice in a row.",
   "start": 70.55,
   "end": 75.15
  },
  {
   "id": "l2b",
   "scene": "loop",
   "show": "One spike can't fool it.",
   "start": 75.47,
   "end": 76.63
  },
  {
   "id": "l3",
   "scene": "loop",
   "show": "3. Score: each slice gets a business score, 0 to 100.",
   "start": 77.05,
   "end": 81.25
  },
  {
   "id": "l4",
   "scene": "loop",
   "show": "4. Decide. Many small cuts beat one big cut. Harm grows faster than the cut.",
   "start": 81.67,
   "end": 87.29
  },
  {
   "id": "l4b",
   "scene": "loop",
   "show": "One slice cut 60%: harm 0.36. Six slices cut 10%: just 0.06.",
   "start": 87.61,
   "end": 95.06
  },
  {
   "id": "l4c",
   "scene": "loop",
   "show": "Life-safety slices are never touched. No slice drops below its minimum.",
   "start": 95.48,
   "end": 99.42
  },
  {
   "id": "l5",
   "scene": "loop",
   "show": "5. Apply the new speed limits on the gateway.",
   "start": 99.84,
   "end": 102.62
  },
  {
   "id": "l6",
   "scene": "loop",
   "show": "6. Restore bandwidth after each recovery window.",
   "start": 103.04,
   "end": 106.18
  },
  {
   "id": "l7",
   "scene": "loop",
   "show": "7. Record a permanent explanation. Nobody can edit or delete it, not even an admin.",
   "start": 106.6,
   "end": 112.15
  },
  {
   "id": "d1",
   "scene": "decision",
   "show": "In the lunch-hour rush, demand hit 1,316 kilobits, with 950 usable.",
   "start": 113.07,
   "end": 118.58
  },
  {
   "id": "d2",
   "scene": "decision",
   "show": "With a safety margin, it had to free 251.5 kilobits.",
   "start": 118.95,
   "end": 122.88
  },
  {
   "id": "d3",
   "scene": "decision",
   "show": "Remember our question? The canteen screens took an 80% cut.",
   "start": 123.35,
   "end": 126.94
  },
  {
   "id": "d4",
   "scene": "decision",
   "show": "Office Wi-Fi lost 32%, the warehouse 24%, CCTV 12%. Patient monitoring: never cut.",
   "start": 127.31,
   "end": 134.02
  },
  {
   "id": "d5",
   "scene": "decision",
   "show": "Factory and lab: untouched. The gateway enforced it 4 seconds later, with no button pressed.",
   "start": 134.39,
   "end": 139.75
  },
  {
   "id": "n1",
   "scene": "new",
   "show": "What's new? Not slicing, not the sharing maths, but the combination.",
   "start": 140.67,
   "end": 144.95
  },
  {
   "id": "n2",
   "scene": "new",
   "show": "Business value, not labels. Small cuts, not one deep cut.",
   "start": 145.32,
   "end": 149.49
  },
  {
   "id": "n3",
   "scene": "new",
   "show": "Safety as a hard rule, not a weight.",
   "start": 149.81,
   "end": 151.84
  },
  {
   "id": "n4",
   "scene": "new",
   "show": "And it is proved on real traffic, every 2 seconds recorded.",
   "start": 152.16,
   "end": 155.04
  },
  {
   "id": "n5",
   "scene": "new",
   "show": "With arbitration off, the clinic waited half a second. On: 23 milliseconds, no loss.",
   "start": 155.41,
   "end": 161.29
  },
  {
   "id": "f1",
   "scene": "future",
   "show": "Today the link is real but small: 1 megabit, shaped in our own software.",
   "start": 162.21,
   "end": 165.97
  },
  {
   "id": "f2",
   "scene": "future",
   "show": "Real traffic, measured delay, phones on a hotspot, and the full engine. 460 tests pass.",
   "start": 166.34,
   "end": 172.62
  },
  {
   "id": "f3",
   "scene": "future",
   "show": "Next: seven phones measured, kernel shaping,",
   "start": 173.14,
   "end": 176.075
  },
  {
   "id": "f4",
   "scene": "future",
   "show": "a real 5G core, and radio slicing.",
   "start": 176.125,
   "end": 178.43
  },
  {
   "id": "f5",
   "scene": "future",
   "show": "When the link is full, it slows down what matters least to the business,",
   "start": 179.25,
   "end": 182.55
  },
  {
   "id": "f6",
   "scene": "future",
   "show": "in small, fair, safe steps. And it explains every decision.",
   "start": 182.6,
   "end": 186.72
  }
 ],
